#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1301 expect=violation domain=TD
#note "Pins the (?!\$) lookaheads, the ONLY thing in PMDA's pattern that rejects a designator with no components: 'P' fails the first lookahead outright, and 'PT' passes it but then leaves the trailing 'T' unmatched. Both fire. This is the fixture that distinguishes PMDA's spelling from a naive ^P.*\$."
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 TDSTOFF=P
#expectViolationAt row=2 TDSTOFF=PT
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TD class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Disease Assessments"
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col TDORDER  type=Num
col TDANCVAR type=Char
col TDSTOFF  type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TD | 1 | RSSTDTC | P
CDISCPILOT01 | TD | 2 | RSSTDTC | PT
